recommendedPlan.change:
- Interface: `interface OnDeviceLyricsTranslator { suspend fun identifyLanguage(text: String): String? /* BCP-47 or null for "und" */; suspend fun isModelDownloaded(lang: String): Boolean; suspend fun translate(lines: List<String>, source: String, target: String): List<String> }`.
- `@Singleton class MlKitLyricsTranslator @Inject constructor() : OnDeviceLyricsTranslator`:
  - language ID: LanguageIdentification.getClient(LanguageIdentificationOptions.Builder().setConfidenceThreshold(0.5f).build()).identifyLanguage(sample).await(), mapping "und" to null;
  - model check: RemoteModelManager.getInstance().isModelDownloaded(TranslateRemoteModel.Builder(lang).build()).await();
  - translation: Translation.getClient(TranslatorOptions.Builder().setSourceLanguage(src).setTargetLanguage(tgt).build()), then downloadModelIfNeeded(DownloadConditions.Builder().build()).await(), then translate(line).await() per unique non-blank line;
  - always close() clients in finally;
  - map language tags with TranslateLanguage.fromLanguageTag(tag), which returns null when unsupported.
- AppModule (object at di/AppModule.kt:75-76): `@Provides fun provideOnDeviceLyricsTranslator(impl: MlKitLyricsTranslator): OnDeviceLyricsTranslator = impl`, so tests can fake it.

