risks:
ML Kit:
- adds native code to each ABI split and a ~30 MB model download per language on first use;
- may collide with TFLite/LiteRT native libs at packaging (check mergeDebugNativeLibs);
- is Google-proprietary, under the ML Kit terms;
- loses cross-line context, so translation quality is per-line;
- language ID is unreliable on short lines, so detect the dominant language on joined text.

Merge conflicts with other Android port items:
- sync-editor port: LyricsSheet, LyricsMoreBottomSheet's 'sync yourself' row (175-178), LyricsSyncEditorOverlay;
- player-controls port: the favourite heart/isFavoriteProvider staleness in BottomToggleRow and GlassPlayerToggleRow;
- glass-expansion port: AdaptiveModalBottomSheet floating flag. Implement it once;
- local-ai port: must keep translateLyricsViaAi → AiStateHolder and not edit the lyrics UI files;
- accent-color port: chrome colours come from the album scheme.

